<div class="simulation-content">
    <div class="simulation-description">
        <h3>Storage Costs and Trading Decisions</h3>
        <p>
            This simulation demonstrates how <strong>storage costs</strong> affect trading decisions and lead to 
            the emergence of preferred intermediary goods. You'll see how different commodities become 
            more or less suitable for indirect trading based on their storage characteristics.
        </p>
        
        <div class="learning-objectives">
            <h4>Learning Objectives</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Understand how storage costs affect trading decisions</li>
                <li>Observe the emergence of preferred intermediary goods</li>
                <li>Learn why some goods become "money" while others don't</li>
                <li>Experience the three-agent circular production economy</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

